# Build products. Everything here is regenerated by `make`.
build/
bin/

# Editor and OS noise.
*.o
*.exe
.vscode/
.idea/
Thumbs.db

# Word owner-lock files, created while a .docx deliverable is open
~$*

# Python bytecode from the generators in tools/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# The paper. `paper/matrixlang.tex` is the submission source and is committed,
# together with the PDF built from it. `paper/main.tex` is the working draft it
# is generated from: same text, plus one comment per stated figure binding it to
# the measurement it reports. Those comments are drafting apparatus, so the draft
# stays local. `make paper` regenerates both.
paper/main.tex
tools/strip_anchors.py

# LaTeX build products. The PDF is committed; the intermediates are not.
paper/*.aux
paper/*.log
paper/*.out
paper/*.fls
paper/*.fdb_latexmk
paper/*.synctex.gz
paper/build.log
